<item><title>Contract 26/67 High Street Rider Main Installation</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> This Contract is for the installation of a new 63mm OD PE80 Full RC water rider main on the northern footpath of High Street Rangiora between King Street and Ashley Street. The pipe is to be sleeved inside of the abandoned DN150 stainless steel which is present under the footpath. The abandoned main has been investigated and found to be clear along its length without bends. Some heavy cleaning of the internal wall is to be undertaken as required to enable installation. Camera footage along the full length of the abandoned main is provided in the appendices. The contract includes several connections to the water network as described in the document.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Waimakariri District Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 21/Oct/2026 04:00 pm (UTC+12:00) Auckland, Wellington time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP2692<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Construction & Operation, Water & Sewage<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 8]]></description>
<link>https://www.vendorpanel.nz/PublicTenderAccess.aspx?id=14a1e7993e444cf58bcf8cab33436eb5s2692</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">14a1e7993e444cf58bcf8cab33436eb5</guid>
<pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 03:13:00 GMT</pubDate>
<category>Construction &amp; Operation</category>
<category>Water &amp; Sewage</category>
</item>
<item><title>Oxford A&amp;P Stormwater Improvement Works and Bay Road Drainage Upgrade</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> This contract covers the construction of a swale, a bund, soakage devices, and the installation of stormwater pipes in Oxford. <br /><br />The main tasks involved in this Contract are:<br /><br />Separable Portion A (SPA): Oxford A&P Stormwater Improvements<br /><br />•	Constructing a bund along the northern and eastern boundaries of the Oxford Agricultural & Pastoral (A&P) Showgrounds.<br /><br />•	Regrading and reshaping of existing swales within the showgrounds. <br /><br />•	Installing an inlet wingwall structure and a new DN450 pipe through 53 and 53A Burnett Street and connecting the pipe into the existing stormwater infrastructure. A DN300 orifice plate will be installed on the inlet to restrict flow into Church Street Reserve, with removal anticipated following downstream upgrades. <br /><br />•	Minor localised lowering works at Reids Lane footpath near southern end of eastern Oxford A&P Showgrounds shelter belt.<br /><br />•	Remove the existing DN300 pipe and supply and install a new DN450 under Chur...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Waimakariri District Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 28/Oct/2026 04:00 pm (UTC+12:00) Auckland, Wellington time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP2691<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Construction & Operation, Water & Sewage<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 9]]></description>
